-# One identity at a time: the ADT tool rejects both options together. The phone identity writes the same /buttons and activation
-# properties with the artwork geometry of phone_model. Three things still stand between this and an iPhone-shaped UI: the installed
-# System is the unchanged iPad7,1 iPadOS 17.7.11 root, and the guide keeps the OS family with that root (iPadOS root stays iPadOS);
-# MobileGestalt caches its answers on the Data volume, keyed by build and platform UUID, so an identity change needs those cached
-# answers cleared; and the UI point scale comes from the offline-legacy-unit-scale boot argument, which publishes /chosen/display-scale
-# that MobileGestalt reads, so artwork-scale-factor = 3 here only matches the screen once that argument says 3 too.
-ipad_identity = false
-phone_identity = true
-phone_model = "iPhone15,2"           # iPhone 14 Pro: root model, target type D72, 1179x2556 pixels at 3x (393 points wide)
